# The build context for the backend image.
#
# Everything here is either rebuilt inside the image, belongs to the other half
# of the repository, or must never enter an image layer at all. The last group
# is the one that matters: a file copied into a layer stays in the image even if
# a later layer deletes it, and `docker history` will still show it.

# --- Never, under any circumstances ----------------------------------------
# Environment files. The templates carry no values and the real ones carry all
# of them, so the whole family is excluded rather than the dangerous half: a
# rule that depends on somebody having named their file correctly is not a rule.
.env
.env.*

# Uploaded files written by the local file store. Customer bytes in a real
# installation, test rubbish here, and neither belongs in an image.
var/

# --- Rebuilt inside the image ----------------------------------------------
target/

# --- Belongs to the other image --------------------------------------------
frontend/

# --- Not needed to compile or to run ---------------------------------------
.git/
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
.claude/
.mcp.json
deploy/
docs/
*.md
phase9-plan.txt
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
